      "raw": "<p>Apostate&#39;s Relic Spirit card states: &quot;<span style=\"color: rgb(119, 119, 119); font-family: arial, sans, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 13px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">When this card is destroyed, move (H) minus 1 Relic cards from the Villain trash into play.&quot;</span></p><p>Other cards that pull from the villain trash,&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">like Return with the Dawn or TCF Stalwart,</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;usually have some sort of instructions about shuffling the trash and revealing cards from the top. Relic Spirit doesn&#39;t have this though, so how do you determine which relics come out? During a game last night we ruled that since the card didn&#39;t specify, the players choose which relics to put into play. Is that a correct interpretation?</span></p>",
